# The First Dependency, a Compromised outcome.
#
# Every line is an ordinary player command through the same API the interface
# uses. Nothing here grants resources or bypasses the daily resolver.

note Day 0: the expedition is affordable from the opening stock, so launch at once.
launch_colonization
step 2

note Day 2: the colony is founded. Staff the Hub for water and put the rest of the
note arriving workers on the colony's first Spaceport.
assign_workers planet=frontier to=@frontier:hub_water count=10
start_construction planet=frontier facility_type=spaceport
assign_workers planet=frontier to=@last count=20
step 3

note Day 5: the port is finished. Staff it from the released construction crew and
note open the supply route. Each package is kept to 100 cargo volume so the colony's
note reduced port service still clears a whole shipment in one day, which is what
note keeps the ideal six-day cycle intact.
assign_workers planet=frontier to=@frontier:spaceport_handling count=20
update_route field=outbound food=65 steel=30 machinery=5
update_route field=return iron_ore=100
update_route field=enable flag=true
step 4

note Day 9: the package has landed. Start the colony's Extraction Site, then switch
note the outbound manifest to food and maintenance machinery.
start_construction planet=frontier facility_type=extraction_site recipe=extraction_iron
assign_workers planet=frontier to=@last count=20
update_route field=outbound food=95 machinery=5
step 6

note Day 15: staff the mine. Frontier now sends ore home while Homeworld sends food
note out: that is the two-way dependence the prototype exists to test.
assign_workers planet=frontier to=@frontier:extraction_iron count=20

note Build the colony's food buffer for the weeks when the freighter serves the front.
until day=70

note Day 70: the freighter is docked at home. Take it off the colonial route now, so
note no scheduled colonial manifest is missed while it is away.
update_route field=enable flag=false
until day=75

note Day 75: the mandate is issued and declined. The civilian economy is never
note interrupted, so the colony thrives, but the final report records political
note compromise rather than a completed term.
respond_to_demand response=decline
update_route field=enable flag=true
until day=120
